<PageTitle>DbnSpool docs: DbnSuite</PageTitle>

<h1>DbnSpool</h1>
<p class="lead">
    An optional worker that keeps <a href="docs/tapes">tapes</a> up to date. It reads your archive of Databento® files,
    builds each new trade date, proves it, and uploads it to a second store, such as a DigitalOcean Space.
</p>

<div class="note"><p>
    <strong>Most people don't need this.</strong> DbnSpool exists for running simulation and testing from a cloud store
    day after day. DbnSync, DbnFetch and DbnClient all work without it, and <code>dbnf tape build</code> makes tapes by
    hand whenever you want some.
</p></div>

